            <ArticleTitle>[Emergency surgical indications in pregnancy (3 rarely encountered cases)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>575-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors evaluated 3 cases of acute abdomen during pregnancy: Spontaneous rupture of splenic artery at 30th gestational week (gw). Torsion of left normal Fallopian tube at 33rd gw. Left adnexal torsion at 36th gw. The symptomatology, the etio-pathology and the anatomo-pathological characteristics of every case wore discussed. In women that are usually young, maternal and fetal exitus in the first case and salpingectomy or adnexectomy in the second and third case can be avoided only thanks to timely surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
